{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For I know whom you bless, etc.</b> This teaches that he was regarded as one whose curse took effect upon the accursed, in the manner that the Sages, blessed be their memory, said: 'Do not take lightly the curse of an ordinary person in your eyes.'" "<b>And know that</b> the sage Rabbi Abraham, of blessed memory, [held that] through the wisdom of the constellations which he knew, when he saw a person's star in decline and his time of evil had arrived, he would curse him; and when the evil came upon him, people would reckon that his curse had caused it. Therefore he schemed to say to the officers of Balak: 'I am not able to transgress the word of HaShem,' for there is no power in a created being to change the deeds of the Creator or His decrees. But the opinion of our Sages, of blessed memory, is not so."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:52.876365235Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}